{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari","id":1186236,"title":"Kitsune and the Temples of Inari","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-15T04:23:56-08:00","id":1186236,"title":"Kitsune and the Temples of Inari","content":"A bit unique among the changing breeds, the Kitsune have a large religious community dedicated to them in a major 1st world country. How exactly are they connected to it? A look at the CB20 book doesn't seem to mention it, did any of the older books do so?<br /> <br /> I have visited the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fushimi_Inari-taisha\" target=\"_blank\">Fushima Inari Temple</a> in Kyoto and it is just massive. You can feel the weight of history and spiritual peace just weighing down on you there. This is the most famous shrine in the nation and millions visit it every year. There are sub shrines connected to this temple all across the country.<br /> <br /> I imagine there being a powerful Caern somewhere on the grounds, and that it is home base to the Kitsune of Kyoto. The shrine and it's temple are run by their kinfolk (who must be quite numerous given how many people it must take to run such a large shrine), as I can't imagine the Kitsune themselves interacting with so many people or doing such mundane work; and I imagine the senior priests among them have mastered some sorcery and are always on the look out for more to share with their brethren and record in their secret library.<br /> <br /> How do you guys envision it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 02-15-2018, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T14:10:24-08:00","id":1186408,"title":"","content":"There's a reason Kitsune have instead of the background Kinfolk they have &quot;clan&quot; as an extended group of people related to them nto so related to them that are cool with them and so on..I'd imagine that many Inari shrines are run by various Kitsune clan as a background, which includes everything from mundane hangers on to kinfolk, to sorcerers and probably some true mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T16:47:17-08:00","id":1186474,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Kitsune of Kyoto must have 5 dots in Clan, Batsu and Go-en for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T03:06:38-08:00","id":1189174,"title":"","content":"Check the Caerns, Places of Power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T18:03:57-08:00","id":1189323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari?p=1189174#post1189174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check the Caerns, Places of Power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh...It's a pre shapeshifters of the east source book and is pretty dated. The kitsune are presented differently then they would be later on. Also, the art is pretty out there even for WTA. Kind of weird that the caren is right there on the middle of a busy bridge. Has some interesting lore about Japanese sorcerers but that's about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 02-24-2018, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T22:00:47-08:00","id":1189345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari?p=1189323#post1189323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh...It's a pre shapeshifters of the east source book and is pretty dated. The kitsune are presented differently then they would be later on. Also, the art is pretty out there even for WTA. Kind of weird that the caren is right there on the middle of a busy bridge. Has some interesting lore about Japanese sorcerers but that's about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Oda Nobunaga received the Embrace, apparently, in addition to later becoming a ghost, per Dark Kingdom of Jade. Who lost a duel against Yu Huang, big time (if it really was the &quot;emperor&quot; at all, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T16:47:50-08:00","id":1190056,"title":"","content":"I knew about his battle with the Jade Emperor - that's what fueled speculation that Yu Huang was actually a Neverborn. I didn't know he became a Kindred. Where was that written?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T22:02:03-08:00","id":1190143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari?p=1190056#post1190056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I knew about his battle with the Jade Emperor - that's what fueled speculation that Yu Huang was actually a Neverborn. I didn't know he became a Kindred. Where was that written?</div> </div> </div> </div>An apparently throwaway line in Caerns: Places of Power, in the chapter just mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T22:10:36-08:00","id":1190148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari?p=1189345#post1189345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, Oda Nobunaga received the Embrace, apparently, in addition to later becoming a ghost, per Dark Kingdom of Jade. Who lost a duel against Yu Huang, big time (if it really was the &quot;emperor&quot; at all, of course).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've always thought Oda Nobunaga would make an excellent Devil Tiger Elder...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T05:19:50-08:00","id":1190208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari?p=1190148#post1190148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've always thought Oda Nobunaga would make an excellent Devil Tiger Elder...</div> </div> </div> </div>The book is so old it predates the Kindred of the East.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T06:46:23-08:00","id":1190248,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari?p=1190143#post1190143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An apparently throwaway line in Caerns: Places of Power, in the chapter just mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Nobunaga appears to also also originally slated to be the Kuei-jin elder of Tokyo. In World of Darkness: Hong Kong on page 108 there's an insane Hakken who works for the Kuei-jin leader of Tokyo, Hakkari. But on one line it calls him Nobunaga (probably an artifact from a find/replace). Still, if we took the idea that Nobunaga is merely pretending to be Hikari, this would mean Nobunaga was brought back as a Kindred, died and turned into a wraith, was then defeated by Yu Huang, had his soul fall into Yomi and then escaped and came back as a Kuei-jin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T12:21:47-08:00","id":1190380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari?p=1190248#post1190248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Interesting. Nobunaga appears to also also originally slated to be the Kuei-jin elder of Tokyo. In World of Darkness: Hong Kong on page 108 there's an insane Hakken who works for the Kuei-jin leader of Tokyo, Hakkari. But on one line it calls him Nobunaga (probably an artifact from a find/replace). Still, if we took the idea that Nobunaga is merely pretending to be Hikari, this would mean Nobunaga was brought back as a Kindred, died and turned into a wraith, was then defeated by Yu Huang, had his soul fall into Yomi and then escaped and came back as a Kuei-jin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt that's how it went; I would expect more retcons of what happened. In large part because if the Neverborn wearing Emperor Qin's ghost like a suit devoured you, you'd probably be ending up in Oblivion - the Grand Maw, with an Orpheus appearance, perhaps, but otherwise, your existence is likely at an absolute end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T15:53:17-08:00","id":1190468,"title":"","content":"Eh...Nobunaga is interesting, but does no one have anything to say about kitsune and the huge religious institution that venerates them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T19:45:13-08:00","id":1190537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari?p=1190468#post1190468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh...Nobunaga is interesting, but does no one have anything to say about kitsune and the huge religious institution that venerates them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that it would venerate them so directly or specifically. They still have Rage, it's still going to be off-putting for a potentially large number of people around them, and they're still going to need to do more lurking than direct dealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T18:59:54-08:00","id":1190873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari?p=1190537#post1190537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know that it would venerate them so directly or specifically. They still have Rage, it's still going to be off-putting for a potentially large number of people around them, and they're still going to need to do more lurking than direct dealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my perhaps limited understanding of the mythology, foxes and kitsune are not really distinguished as seperate things. The word kitsune literally means fox and it is believed that any fox that lives long enough will eventually learn to shapeshift, learn magic and grow more tails. Thus the veneration of foxes at temples of Inari extends to venerating the werefoxes of the World of Darkness by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T20:38:11-08:00","id":1190895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari?p=1190873#post1190873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my perhaps limited understanding of the mythology, foxes and kitsune are not really distinguished as seperate things. The word kitsune literally means fox and it is believed that any fox that lives long enough will eventually learn to shapeshift, learn magic and grow more tails. Thus the veneration of foxes at temples of Inari extends to venerating the werefoxes of the World of Darkness by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, Rage and The Curse put a spanner in the works. If you have it, humans with lower Willpower don't want to have anything to do with you. So while an awful lot of people might venerate figures of legend, they might not recognize the Fera known as Kitsune as being &quot;proper&quot; foxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T22:06:21-08:00","id":1190906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari?p=1190895#post1190895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, Rage and The Curse put a spanner in the works. If you have it, humans with lower Willpower don't want to have anything to do with you. So while an awful lot of people might venerate figures of legend, they might not recognize the Fera known as Kitsune as being &quot;proper&quot; foxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's why these temples would be run by their kinfolk. Also, Kitsune rage tends to be lower than garou IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T01:14:12-08:00","id":1190920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1186236-kitsune-and-the-temples-of-inari?p=1190906#post1190906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's why these temples would be run by their kinfolk. Also, Kitsune rage tends to be lower than garou IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eji have one less Rage than Ahroun (which is still enough to cause problems), but their lowest Auspices have a basement rating of 2, so not really by enough to matter. That's also the bare minimum possessed by a fox of a given auspice; older Kitsune will likely feel the need to stoke those flames a bit higher, or possibly end up facing situations that would drive it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}